Harlan Supply Co.'s account didn't get fixed by an idea Dana had.

3
00:00:06,384 --> 00:00:11,052
It got fixed by eleven actual documents Sam built, one section at a time, starting

4
00:00:11,052 --> 00:00:14,012
with a single page stating her price and her margin.

5
00:00:14,012 --> 00:00:16,175
That's what you're about to build too.

6
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:20,843
Every section here ends in a workshop, and every workshop produces one artifact: a

7
00:00:20,843 --> 00:00:25,056
real document you'll use on a real account, not a worksheet you file away.

8
00:00:25,056 --> 00:00:28,016
Skip the workshops and you'll still learn the ideas.

9
00:00:28,016 --> 00:00:30,635
You just won't have anything to run on Monday.

10
00:00:30,635 --> 00:00:34,904
So here's the map: what you're building, and which lecture hands it to you.

11
00:00:35,454 --> 00:00:39,959
That's the full set, and notice the shape of it before you notice the details.

12
00:00:39,959 --> 00:00:44,811
Two artifacts before you generate anything: the hook matrix, a grid of opening lines

13
00:00:44,811 --> 00:00:47,468
proven to stop a scroll, and the brief itself.

14
00:00:47,468 --> 00:00:50,760
Two while you're generating, including a UGC video brief.

15
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:55,612
UGC just means it's styled like an ordinary customer's phone footage, not a polished

16
00:00:55,612 --> 00:00:56,190
studio ad.

17
00:00:56,190 --> 00:01:00,059
One artifact exists purely to stop a bad ad before it spends money.

18
00:01:00,059 --> 00:01:04,565
Two for running the test itself, two for reading what it told you, and two for

19
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:07,048
turning one test into an ongoing operation.

20
00:01:07,048 --> 00:01:11,727
Most people building this by hand skip straight to generation, because that's the

21
00:01:11,727 --> 00:01:12,536
exciting part.

22
00:01:12,536 --> 00:01:16,579
The order above is deliberate, and it's the order that actually works.

23
00:01:17,129 --> 00:01:19,438
Here's the shape across the whole course.

24
00:01:19,438 --> 00:01:24,168
The first two sections are judgement: why AI creative changes the economics, and the

25
00:01:24,168 --> 00:01:27,547
brief that decides whether generation is worth doing at all.

26
00:01:27,547 --> 00:01:32,221
The next three are production: statics, meaning still-image ad variants rather than

27
00:01:32,221 --> 00:01:36,444
video, then moving video, then getting the same set to perform on different

28
00:01:36,444 --> 00:01:37,007
