34
00:01:53,043 --> 00:01:55,006
One honest note before you go further.

35
00:01:55,006 --> 00:01:58,467
Nothing here removes the need to spend real money to find a winner.

36
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:02,599
That part is unavoidable, and any course that tells you otherwise is selling you

37
00:02:02,599 --> 00:02:03,116
something.

38
00:02:03,116 --> 00:02:07,197
What the system in this course does is stop you spending on ads that were never

39
00:02:07,197 --> 00:02:08,850
going to win in the first place.

40
00:02:08,850 --> 00:02:13,137
That's a smaller promise than "never spend money", and it's the one that's actually

41
00:02:13,137 --> 00:02:13,395
true.

42
00:02:13,945 --> 00:02:18,201
Here's the one thing to do before you go any further, and it takes two minutes.

43
00:02:18,201 --> 00:02:22,565
Open a note and write down the product or account you'll actually run this course

44
00:02:22,565 --> 00:02:25,151
against: yours, a client's, whatever you've got.

45
00:02:25,151 --> 00:02:29,676
Every one of those eleven artifacts is built to hold a real price and a real margin,

46
00:02:29,676 --> 00:02:33,609
the way Harlan Supply Co.'s brief eventually holds Dana's actual numbers.

47
00:02:33,609 --> 00:02:37,057
Without a real account in mind, you'll be filling in a template.

48
00:02:37,057 --> 00:02:40,127
With one, you'll be building something you use on Monday.

49
00:02:40,127 --> 00:02:43,683
Next lecture is short, and it's the one everything else hangs off.

50
00:02:43,683 --> 00:02:48,208
After that, you'll do the exercise I mentioned: a real ad set, your own guess, and a

51
00:02:48,208 --> 00:02:50,633
